WEBVTT

00:16.934 --> 00:18.519
[Boyd] Previously on From...

00:18.602 --> 00:22.523
Miranda painted things
she saw here.

00:22.606 --> 00:27.027
One of those paintings was of
a man in a yellow suit.

00:29.697 --> 00:31.574
[Victor] I thought
he was just like us.

00:31.657 --> 00:33.659
-[groaning]
-[bones crunching]

00:33.743 --> 00:35.411
[Victor]
But he wasn't like us.

00:35.494 --> 00:39.206
When I found Mom out by
the Bottle Tree, I saw him.

00:39.290 --> 00:40.374
[gasps]

00:40.458 --> 00:41.625
He was eating her.

00:44.628 --> 00:46.297
[glasses clink]

00:46.380 --> 00:48.716
Have you ever wondered if maybe
this is all just a dream?

00:50.593 --> 00:55.556
[screaming]

00:55.639 --> 00:57.725
That thing I carried
inside me... I still feel it.

00:57.808 --> 00:58.726
Like we're connected.

00:58.809 --> 01:02.229
Part of me feels
what he feels.

01:02.313 --> 01:03.773
[grunting with effort]

01:05.566 --> 01:07.568
[Tabitha] There's something
about those dolls.

01:07.651 --> 01:10.196
I think I've seen
them before.

01:10.279 --> 01:12.865
-[smashing]
-[screaming]

01:12.948 --> 01:14.241
-[choking]
-[flesh tearing]

01:14.325 --> 01:15.618
[grunts]

01:17.161 --> 01:18.579
I remembered.

01:18.662 --> 01:20.581
I remembered
how to hurt them.

01:23.459 --> 01:25.753
This is where the children
were sacrificed.

01:25.836 --> 01:28.297
Tell me how we save them when
we've already failed!

01:28.380 --> 01:32.134
You want me to help plan a
suicide mission because

01:32.218 --> 01:34.512
you think the bones of those
children are buried down there!

01:34.595 --> 01:36.847
Yes!
There was a hidden door.

01:36.931 --> 01:39.767
Do remember seeing any doors in
the basement of Colony House?

01:39.850 --> 01:42.269
[Boyd] You want me to go down
in those tunnels!

01:42.353 --> 01:44.563
Then show me
the fucking door!

01:44.646 --> 01:45.689
[shouts with effort]

01:45.773 --> 01:48.859
-Holy shit.
-We're gonna need a plan.

01:57.493 --> 01:58.786
[breathing heavily]

02:00.913 --> 02:04.875
[thudding]

02:06.377 --> 02:08.294
-Any luck?
-[Randall] Not yet.

02:13.008 --> 02:14.218
I'm gonna
break it down.

02:14.301 --> 02:15.469
No.
You know what?

02:15.553 --> 02:19.306
If it's sealed,
that's probably for the best.

02:19.390 --> 02:21.267
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

02:22.935 --> 02:24.687
[hammering]

02:33.696 --> 02:35.823
Just in case.

02:35.906 --> 02:39.451
Our lives are
fuckin' weird, man.

02:39.535 --> 02:41.579
Yeah, they are.

02:43.747 --> 02:47.251
[indistinct chatter]

02:48.460 --> 02:49.378
[Boyd] Nothing?

02:49.461 --> 02:50.921
He's not upstairs.

02:51.005 --> 02:52.923
Could be that he, uh--

02:54.925 --> 02:55.968
Never mind.

02:56.051 --> 02:57.595
Evening.

02:59.889 --> 03:01.223
-He's drunk.
-Yup.

03:01.307 --> 03:02.892
You really think now
is the best time to--

03:02.975 --> 03:04.935
I don't have a choice.

03:06.478 --> 03:07.897
Well, do you want me
to come with you?

03:07.980 --> 03:09.189
No, I got it.

03:12.526 --> 03:13.694
Henry.

03:13.777 --> 03:15.362
What can I do you for?

03:15.446 --> 03:19.199
Hey, do you, uh, mind comin'
upstairs and having a word?

03:20.284 --> 03:21.243
What's wrong?

03:21.327 --> 03:22.536
Nothing, nothing.

03:22.620 --> 03:23.704
Is Victor okay?

03:23.787 --> 03:25.539
Victor's fine.
Look, I just--

03:25.623 --> 03:27.541
Uh, there's something
I need to tell everyone.

03:27.625 --> 03:28.876
But it's something
that I think

03:28.959 --> 03:30.753
you and Victor
need to hear first.

03:30.836 --> 03:32.880
So, I just wanna talk to
the two of you; that's all.

03:32.963 --> 03:34.548
All right.

03:34.632 --> 03:36.341
-Whoa, whoa!
-No, I'm fine!

03:36.425 --> 03:37.426
You sure?

03:37.509 --> 03:38.844
I need to say it again?

03:56.654 --> 03:59.239
Are those Dad's shirts?

03:59.323 --> 04:01.659
Yeah.

04:01.742 --> 04:04.036
Sometimes I like to look
at his stuff too.

04:04.119 --> 04:05.245
[sniffling]

04:08.499 --> 04:10.417
Julie's home.

04:13.629 --> 04:14.838
Okay.

04:16.673 --> 04:18.007
[inhaling]

04:19.802 --> 04:21.261
Let's go talk, okay?

04:24.515 --> 04:26.433
Giant dolls?

04:26.517 --> 04:28.727
Mom was the one
who killed it.

04:28.811 --> 04:32.564
She stabbed it with
a voodoo totem.

04:32.648 --> 04:34.358
And how did you know
that would work?

04:35.693 --> 04:38.529
Well, I um...

04:42.366 --> 04:43.867
I remembered.

04:43.951 --> 04:45.411
Remembered what?

04:48.747 --> 04:51.375
There's something
I need to tell you both.

04:51.457 --> 04:53.377
And it's something

04:53.460 --> 04:57.381
that's been very
hard for me to...

04:57.464 --> 04:58.799
to understand.

04:58.882 --> 05:00.009
To believe.

05:00.092 --> 05:03.595
Mom, whatever it is, just--
just say it.

05:08.726 --> 05:10.853
I've been here before.

05:10.936 --> 05:13.397
Many, many times.

05:13.480 --> 05:14.982
All the way back
to the beginning.

05:19.069 --> 05:21.989
The last time I was here,
I was Miranda.

05:22.072 --> 05:24.533
I was Victor's mother.

05:25.868 --> 05:28.037
Are you insane?

05:28.120 --> 05:29.538
Henry--

05:29.621 --> 05:32.624
I'm not listening to this.

05:32.707 --> 05:37.046
Do you have any idea what you
just-- how dare you?

05:37.129 --> 05:38.130
How--

05:38.213 --> 05:39.631
Maybe you should just
sit down.

05:39.715 --> 05:40.674
Don't!

05:40.758 --> 05:43.719
You don't tell me
what to do!

05:43.802 --> 05:45.846
You come in here

05:45.929 --> 05:49.516
and you say those things?

05:49.600 --> 05:53.520
That my wife-- no.

05:53.604 --> 05:55.439
Victor, let's go.

05:55.522 --> 05:58.442
You don't have to listen
to this.

05:58.525 --> 06:00.611
-[door opening]
-It's okay, Dad.

06:00.694 --> 06:02.529
It's okay?
It's not okay!

06:02.613 --> 06:03.947
All right,
why don't we all--

06:04.031 --> 06:05.532
No!

06:05.616 --> 06:07.034
No more.

06:08.619 --> 06:09.870
[door closing]

06:11.580 --> 06:15.834
Victor, do you understand
everything I said?

06:17.252 --> 06:19.004
No one's claiming
that Tabitha is--

06:19.088 --> 06:21.590
when I said she was here before,
that she was your mother,

06:21.673 --> 06:22.883
you have to understand--

06:22.966 --> 06:26.053
Please stop. I don't want you
to talk anymore.

06:27.513 --> 06:28.847
Okay.

06:30.974 --> 06:33.852
I...

06:33.936 --> 06:35.437
I guess I'll--

06:35.521 --> 06:37.815
We need to find out about
the man in yellow.

06:39.900 --> 06:42.778
What does this have to do with
the man in yellow?

06:42.861 --> 06:48.492
Everything. If he's back--

06:48.575 --> 06:51.453
it could all
be happening again.

06:58.710 --> 07:03.632
["Que Sera, Sera (Whatever Will
Be, Will Be)" plays]

07:08.637 --> 07:13.433
♪ When I was just a little boy ♪

07:13.517 --> 07:15.811
♪ I asked my father ♪

07:15.894 --> 07:17.563
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

07:19.648 --> 07:21.942
♪ "Will I be handsome?" ♪

07:22.025 --> 07:24.444
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

07:24.528 --> 07:28.532
♪ Here's what he said to me ♪

07:28.615 --> 07:31.493
♪ Que sera sera ♪

07:32.744 --> 07:35.914
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

07:37.666 --> 07:41.670
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

07:41.753 --> 07:44.548
♪ Que sera sera ♪

07:46.800 --> 07:49.720
♪ What will be will be ♪

07:59.062 --> 08:03.901
♪ Now I have
children of my own ♪

08:03.984 --> 08:06.236
♪ They ask their father ♪

08:06.320 --> 08:09.990
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

08:10.073 --> 08:12.618
♪ "Will I be pretty?" ♪

08:12.701 --> 08:14.995
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

08:15.078 --> 08:17.539
♪ I tell them tenderly ♪

08:19.082 --> 08:21.710
♪ Que sera sera ♪

08:23.170 --> 08:26.506
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

08:28.175 --> 08:32.095
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

08:32.179 --> 08:34.722
♪ Que sera sera ♪

08:37.226 --> 08:40.145
♪ What will be will be ♪

08:42.397 --> 08:45.275
♪ Que sera sera ♪

09:00.040 --> 09:04.670
If you and Tabitha were here
before, does that mean--

09:04.753 --> 09:09.132
were we all here before?

09:09.216 --> 09:10.259
Uh, no.

09:10.342 --> 09:12.219
I don't think so.

09:12.302 --> 09:14.137
Then what the fuck
are we all doing here?

09:15.806 --> 09:20.060
These, these children that were
sacrificed...

09:21.019 --> 09:26.108
...they have been crying out
to Tabitha and me for help,

09:26.191 --> 09:27.693
for all these years,

09:27.776 --> 09:30.362
and that cry,
I think on some level,

09:30.445 --> 09:31.989
maybe you heard it too.

09:32.072 --> 09:34.241
Can we just pause for a second
and talk about the fact

09:34.324 --> 09:37.577
that this is all coming out of
a mushroom trip?

09:37.661 --> 09:40.080
I mean, how is this different
than any of the insane theories

09:40.163 --> 09:42.374
people have had about
this place?

09:42.457 --> 09:44.668
Because of the door
in the basement.

09:44.751 --> 09:46.086
The door behind the wall.

09:46.169 --> 09:48.630
Look, Kristi, I was the first
person to call bullshit

09:48.714 --> 09:50.757
on all of this, okay,
but the truth is,

09:50.841 --> 09:52.342
Jade saw something
in that trip

09:52.426 --> 09:54.386
he couldn't
have possibly known.

09:54.469 --> 09:57.347
But how do we know
this isn't just...

09:57.431 --> 09:59.766
I mean, this place puts a lot
of weird shit in our heads.

09:59.850 --> 10:00.934
I know.

10:01.018 --> 10:02.894
Believe me,
I've thought of that too.

10:02.978 --> 10:05.230
So, how is this
any different?

10:05.314 --> 10:08.066
Because of what they did
to Jim.

10:08.150 --> 10:13.697
That message on the wall:
"Knowledge comes at a cost."

10:13.780 --> 10:16.867
It's possible that Jim died

10:16.950 --> 10:21.330
because of what Tabitha
and Jade remembered.

10:21.413 --> 10:23.790
Look, that message was meant
to scare us.

10:23.874 --> 10:28.920
But I think the message tells
us something else.

10:29.004 --> 10:30.756
That we are close.

10:30.839 --> 10:34.384
For the first time, we are close
to figuring this place out.

10:36.011 --> 10:38.138
When your enemy
threatens you, right,

10:38.221 --> 10:40.849
tries to scare you,

10:40.932 --> 10:43.393
that means
they are scared of you.

10:43.477 --> 10:46.146
[Bakta] And you think this
place is scared of us

10:46.229 --> 10:48.231
digging up the bones
of these children,

10:48.315 --> 10:50.817
because that could be
what gets us home?

10:50.901 --> 10:52.110
Yes.

10:59.993 --> 11:01.161
I guess you told them.

11:01.244 --> 11:02.746
Henry--

11:02.829 --> 11:05.248
It is-- it isn't true.

11:05.332 --> 11:06.750
Henry.

11:06.833 --> 11:08.377
Whatever-- whatever
he said about my wife,

11:08.460 --> 11:12.881
about Tabitha, about him,

11:12.964 --> 11:14.299
it isn't true!

11:14.383 --> 11:15.967
What you are doing...

11:16.051 --> 11:17.010
Okay.

11:17.094 --> 11:18.428
...it isn't right.

11:22.432 --> 11:23.433
I got it.

11:26.812 --> 11:28.855
Henry, wait.

11:28.939 --> 11:30.816
Miranda was right!

11:30.899 --> 11:33.318
You!
Don't you say her name!

11:33.402 --> 11:35.445
Listen to me;
saving the children

11:35.529 --> 11:37.155
is the only way
to get everyone home.

11:37.239 --> 11:38.365
No!

11:38.448 --> 11:40.033
We are trying to finish
what she started!

11:40.117 --> 11:43.203
No!
No, you listen to me.

11:43.286 --> 11:45.372
You may think
you're helping people.

11:45.455 --> 11:49.709
You may think you're smart
enough to get everyone home,

11:49.793 --> 11:51.211
but I promise you,

11:51.294 --> 11:55.048
the only thing you will cause
is pain.

11:55.132 --> 11:58.718
You cannot save dead things!

11:58.802 --> 12:00.846
No matter how fucking smart
you think you are.

12:04.391 --> 12:05.725
Hey.

12:07.227 --> 12:09.062
Give him some time.

12:09.146 --> 12:11.148
He'll come around.

12:11.231 --> 12:12.899
We got things to do.

12:12.983 --> 12:14.234
Yeah.

12:29.291 --> 12:31.334
-[coughs]
-[door opening]

12:36.923 --> 12:38.341
What are you doing?

12:38.425 --> 12:40.969
Nothing.

12:41.052 --> 12:43.472
Julie, I can smell it
through the window.

12:47.309 --> 12:49.936
It just--
it helps me process things.

12:50.020 --> 12:52.272
Okay?

12:52.355 --> 12:53.565
Seriously?

12:53.648 --> 12:55.233
After everything you told us
last night,

12:55.317 --> 12:56.985
this is what you're gonna
hang up on?

12:57.068 --> 12:58.361
Do you want Ethan
to see this?

12:58.445 --> 13:00.280
[Ethan] See what?

13:00.363 --> 13:01.531
Nothing, nothing.

13:03.408 --> 13:05.118
So, is Victor
my brother now?

13:05.202 --> 13:06.495
[Tabitha] What?

13:06.578 --> 13:08.788
Well, if you're Miranda,

13:08.872 --> 13:12.334
then wouldn't that make
me and Victor brothers?

13:12.417 --> 13:15.128
It's not real, Ethan.

13:15.212 --> 13:16.838
What?

13:16.922 --> 13:19.049
Look, Mom, I know you and Jade
think that you've unlocked

13:19.132 --> 13:22.135
this big mystery about
this place but...

13:22.219 --> 13:23.553
it's not real.

13:25.180 --> 13:27.057
This place
doesn't give us real.

13:27.140 --> 13:30.477
It gives us fucked-up,
twisted ideas.

13:30.560 --> 13:33.271
Okay, okay, Julie,
listen to me.

13:33.355 --> 13:37.984
If I had any doubt,
about anything,

13:38.068 --> 13:40.612
I wouldn't have
said anything.

13:40.695 --> 13:43.323
Jade and Boyd wouldn't have
told everyone at Colony House.

13:43.406 --> 13:45.158
-They told people?
-Yes!

13:45.242 --> 13:47.869
-Are you insane?
-This is how we could go home!

13:47.953 --> 13:49.996
Mom! I wish people would just
stop with that shit.

13:50.080 --> 13:51.540
Where are you going?

13:51.623 --> 13:52.999
Somewhere Ethan
won't see.

13:53.083 --> 13:55.252
-What does that mean?
-Nothing. Julie!

13:55.335 --> 13:56.461
[Julie] What?

13:58.588 --> 14:01.216
I need to know you're okay.

14:03.343 --> 14:05.011
I'm not okay.

14:08.265 --> 14:10.058
But I'm not gonna
hurt myself.

14:11.476 --> 14:12.435
So...

14:25.156 --> 14:27.617
Victor's here.

14:32.622 --> 14:33.623
Hello.

14:38.628 --> 14:41.047
Hi, Victor.

14:41.131 --> 14:45.969
I need-- I need to find out
about the man in yellow.

14:49.431 --> 14:52.517
That means that I have to do
something scary.

14:52.601 --> 14:55.604
Will you please
come with me?

15:00.650 --> 15:03.903
I'm saying we got one shot
at this.

15:03.987 --> 15:06.573
So we need to ask every
question we can think of

15:06.656 --> 15:09.284
and then we need
to ask them again.

15:09.367 --> 15:12.120
So, beside the three of us,
who's been in the tunnels?

15:12.203 --> 15:14.080
Victor for sure.

15:14.164 --> 15:16.041
Tabitha, when the house
collapsed.

15:16.124 --> 15:18.084
Great.
That's a start.

15:18.168 --> 15:20.170
We need all the info we can
get on the layout.

15:20.253 --> 15:23.256
Uh, map it, sketch it--
whatever you need to do.

15:23.340 --> 15:25.425
I don't care.
I wanna know every entrance

15:25.508 --> 15:27.218
and every exit
to that chamber,

15:27.302 --> 15:29.054
how long we need to dig,

15:29.137 --> 15:33.058
and then we figure out how
not to get ourselves killed.

15:35.185 --> 15:36.603
Right?
Talk to Randall.

15:36.686 --> 15:38.063
About what?

15:38.146 --> 15:39.439
He spent a lot of time
on the bus

15:39.522 --> 15:41.608
watching those things come
out of the woods at night.

15:41.691 --> 15:44.653
So, we need to get as much intel
as we can on their behaviors,

15:44.736 --> 15:47.656
their patterns-- at the very
least a headcount.

15:47.739 --> 15:49.658
All right, if we're going
into the nest,

15:49.741 --> 15:52.369
I wanna know exactly how many
we're dealing with. Right.

15:52.452 --> 15:54.412
This place isn't gonna make
it easy, you know.

15:54.496 --> 15:56.498
Once we push,
it's gonna push back hard.

15:56.581 --> 15:58.583
Yeah. I got an idea
about that, so...

16:00.377 --> 16:01.586
What's wrong with your hand?

16:02.796 --> 16:04.631
Nothing, nothing.

16:04.714 --> 16:06.341
Look, we just told
everybody out there

16:06.424 --> 16:08.009
some genuinely fucked-up shit.

16:08.093 --> 16:10.303
The longer they get to stew on
it, the greater the chance

16:10.387 --> 16:12.722
somebody gets in their head
to do something stupid.

16:12.806 --> 16:17.227
So, we need to do this smart,
but we gotta do it fast.

16:18.812 --> 16:20.146
Let's get to work.

16:20.230 --> 16:21.731
[Kenny]
Yes, sir.

16:24.567 --> 16:28.196
[clicking]

16:30.198 --> 16:32.075
Simpler times, huh?

16:34.369 --> 16:35.662
[sighs]

16:35.745 --> 16:38.123
That wasn't just busy work
you gave me, huh?

16:38.206 --> 16:39.582
No.

16:39.665 --> 16:41.459
I was hoping you might find
something useful

16:41.543 --> 16:44.170
about Tabitha and Jade.

16:44.254 --> 16:46.172
You really think
that they've been--

16:46.256 --> 16:49.551
Look, I-- We're talking
about reincarnation here, okay?

16:49.634 --> 16:52.011
-That's a whole different--
-Yeah...

16:52.095 --> 16:53.555
Yeah.

16:53.638 --> 16:55.515
Look, if you're going down into
those tunnels,

16:55.598 --> 16:56.516
you're gonna need help.

16:56.599 --> 16:58.184
Yes, I am.
And you and me,

16:58.268 --> 17:00.228
we're gonna talk about that
when the time comes.

17:00.311 --> 17:02.439
But right now, I need you back
in that basement--

17:02.522 --> 17:03.732
No, Boyd, I gotta--

17:03.815 --> 17:05.525
You know, this is not just--
not just you.

17:05.608 --> 17:06.984
We need a whole team
down there.

17:07.068 --> 17:10.070
And we need a second team at
the diner in the storerooms.

17:10.155 --> 17:11.531
Looking for what?

17:11.614 --> 17:13.742
Anything you can tell me about
a man in a yellow suit.

17:13.825 --> 17:16.118
A man--

17:16.202 --> 17:17.537
Who the fuck is that?

17:17.619 --> 17:20.540
Yeah. I'm hoping something that
you find might tell me--

17:20.623 --> 17:22.541
You sure you're not just
looking for something

17:22.625 --> 17:25.044
to keep everyone's minds off of
how fucking crazy this is?

17:25.127 --> 17:26.546
Listen, if we're
gonna do this,

17:26.628 --> 17:29.466
we need to know exactly what is
out there waiting for us.

17:39.309 --> 17:41.102
Is that all
you can give me?

17:41.186 --> 17:42.687
A man in a yellow suit?

17:42.771 --> 17:45.398
We know that he was here
in the late '70s.

17:45.482 --> 17:47.734
When Victor was a kid.

17:47.817 --> 17:50.153
[sighs]
That's a start, I guess.

17:52.280 --> 17:53.531
[grunts]

17:53.615 --> 17:54.532
[gasps]

17:54.616 --> 17:56.618
Simpler times.

17:56.701 --> 17:57.660
Yeah.

18:05.460 --> 18:09.130
[clicking]

18:11.633 --> 18:13.676
[ominous music plays]

18:23.228 --> 18:27.315
[clicking]

18:27.398 --> 18:30.735
[door opening and closing]

18:32.237 --> 18:33.613
How's she doing?

18:33.696 --> 18:35.490
Cognitively,
she seems fine.

18:35.573 --> 18:38.618
As far as any damage, I got
the ultrasound from the clinic.

18:38.701 --> 18:39.828
And?

18:39.911 --> 18:42.121
I didn't see anything
catastrophic,

18:42.205 --> 18:46.292
but without a CT or an MRI...
yeah,

18:46.376 --> 18:48.711
the hard part is just gonna be
getting her to take it easy.

18:48.795 --> 18:50.129
Yeah.

18:50.213 --> 18:52.215
-Well, you can go see her.
-Kristi!

18:52.298 --> 18:54.300
-What?
-What? Come on.

18:54.384 --> 18:56.678
You should've told me
about Jade and Tabitha.

18:56.761 --> 18:58.555
We're supposed to be
in this together.

18:58.638 --> 18:59.931
No, yeah. We are.
We are.

19:00.014 --> 19:01.516
-But-- We are.
-[sighs]

19:01.599 --> 19:02.725
We are.

19:04.519 --> 19:05.645
We are.

19:06.896 --> 19:09.274
-How are you feeling?
-I'm good.

19:09.357 --> 19:11.276
-And the tremors?
-I'm dealing with them.

19:11.359 --> 19:12.819
Still seeing things
that aren't there?

19:12.902 --> 19:15.405
No.
No, just the one time.

19:17.323 --> 19:19.576
You've got a lot of people's
lives in your hands, Boyd.

19:19.659 --> 19:21.661
Mm. Yeah.

19:21.744 --> 19:23.496
Come to
the clinic.

19:23.580 --> 19:25.206
I wanna do an exam.

19:25.290 --> 19:27.333
Yeah. Yeah.

19:32.505 --> 19:34.632
[knocking]

19:34.716 --> 19:35.800
Yeah.

19:37.802 --> 19:39.429
Hey.

19:41.723 --> 19:43.766
How you feeling?

19:43.850 --> 19:45.852
Better than you look.

19:45.935 --> 19:47.979
Maybe you should be the one
lying here.

19:48.062 --> 19:49.856
Yeah, maybe.

19:49.939 --> 19:52.358
Heard you had a big meeting
downstairs.

19:52.442 --> 19:54.360
Yes, we did.

19:54.444 --> 19:56.821
So you thought it would be
a good idea

19:56.905 --> 19:59.365
to gather up a house full of
emotionally unstable people

19:59.449 --> 20:02.327
and spend the night talking
about reincarnation

20:02.410 --> 20:04.370
and the bones
of dead children.

20:04.454 --> 20:06.956
-I didn't have a choice.
-[Donna] Right.

20:07.040 --> 20:09.918
Because you took a fucking
sledgehammer to my wall.

20:12.420 --> 20:14.380
That door something we should
worry about?

20:14.464 --> 20:16.716
No, we tried to open it;
it's sealed.

20:16.799 --> 20:18.301
Jade said it leads
to the tunnels,

20:18.384 --> 20:21.971
so we put an extra talisman
on it just to be safe.

20:24.390 --> 20:25.350
You bury Roger yet?

20:26.893 --> 20:28.311
He's still in the shed.

20:28.394 --> 20:29.687
[Donna]
Oh, Jesus, Boyd--

20:29.771 --> 20:30.897
We need to pick a new spot.

20:30.980 --> 20:33.399
-For what?
-For burying people!

20:33.483 --> 20:36.402
The cemetery--
The cemetery's full.

20:36.486 --> 20:38.363
We were pushing it with Jim
and the pastor.

20:38.446 --> 20:41.240
Got any more good news
you wanna bring me?

20:41.324 --> 20:42.575
Look.

20:42.659 --> 20:44.953
I need you to tell me
everything you can

20:45.036 --> 20:47.747
about those totems you brought
back from the settlement.

20:47.830 --> 20:50.416
The one Tabitha used
to kill that doll.

20:50.500 --> 20:51.793
I told you
everything already.

20:51.876 --> 20:53.836
Tell me again.

20:53.920 --> 20:55.463
Why?

20:55.546 --> 20:57.465
Because tonight I'm gonna find
out if they work

20:57.548 --> 20:59.384
on those things
that come out of the woods.

20:59.467 --> 21:02.345
That's a fucking
terrible idea.

21:02.428 --> 21:06.391
Let's say you actually kill one
of those things.

21:07.850 --> 21:11.479
Apparently,
they don't even stay dead.

21:11.562 --> 21:13.606
You ready to risk another one
of our people

21:13.690 --> 21:15.733
going through what Fatima
just went through?

21:15.817 --> 21:19.487
What I want is to keep our
people safe in those tunnels.

21:19.570 --> 21:22.615
So, let's just deal with one
problem at a time.

21:22.699 --> 21:24.450
Okay?

21:24.534 --> 21:26.619
Okay, so I need three people
with Elgin

21:26.703 --> 21:28.579
to go through the storeroom
at the diner and then

21:28.663 --> 21:30.707
the rest of you are gonna be
in the basement with me.

21:30.790 --> 21:32.834
And, remember, be quick
but be thorough, okay?

21:32.917 --> 21:34.502
We got this.

21:37.714 --> 21:38.881
You're gonna
go with him.

21:38.965 --> 21:40.550
Sir, you're
over here.

21:58.818 --> 22:01.112
[door creaking]

22:01.195 --> 22:04.907
What are you doing
in here?

22:06.451 --> 22:08.911
Did you know anything
about him?

22:08.995 --> 22:11.330
About Roger?

22:11.414 --> 22:13.332
Uh, yeah.

22:14.500 --> 22:16.502
Uh, gardening.

22:16.586 --> 22:18.504
Yeah, just about every
conversation we had

22:18.588 --> 22:21.507
was about his... his garden
back home.

22:23.468 --> 22:25.678
My mom used to tell me that
when people die,

22:25.762 --> 22:28.139
they just go somewhere else.

22:28.222 --> 22:30.683
She didn't really believe in
heaven or hell;

22:30.767 --> 22:32.727
she just believed
that death was a transition

22:32.810 --> 22:34.103
to another place we
couldn't see from here.

22:37.148 --> 22:39.025
I remember how much comfort
that brought me

22:39.108 --> 22:41.861
when she passed away.

22:41.944 --> 22:45.156
But whatever that place is,

22:45.239 --> 22:47.033
Roger doesn't get to go.

22:49.577 --> 22:51.871
Because he's still here.

22:51.954 --> 22:54.082
They're all still here.

23:01.130 --> 23:04.634
Whatever they're doing to find
those bones, we need to help.

23:12.642 --> 23:13.935
[Boyd] Look, so we know

23:14.018 --> 23:15.937
they tend to spread out
down the street, right?

23:16.020 --> 23:18.773
And according to Randall,
they've got patterns;

23:18.856 --> 23:20.399
some of them have
nightly rituals

23:20.483 --> 23:21.651
and we can use that.

23:21.734 --> 23:25.154
So, say we catch one of them
right here.

23:25.238 --> 23:27.406
Right, we aim fast and dirty,
turn around,

23:27.490 --> 23:28.825
head right back into
the station.

23:28.908 --> 23:29.826
-Right?
-[Ellis] Sure.

23:29.909 --> 23:31.786
And even-- even if--

23:31.869 --> 23:34.205
even if the station
is blocked,

23:34.288 --> 23:37.416
we got plenty of exit routes
all up and down the street.

23:37.500 --> 23:39.085
'Kay, and what if
something goes wrong?

23:39.168 --> 23:41.212
Then we improvise.

23:41.295 --> 23:45.091
Look, those things are used to
us cowering inside our houses,

23:45.174 --> 23:47.426
locking the doors,
lowering the blinds,

23:47.510 --> 23:48.886
trying to ignore them.

23:48.970 --> 23:49.971
The last thing they expect

23:50.054 --> 23:52.140
is for one of us to head
straight at them.

23:52.223 --> 23:56.144
The bottom line is,
these things can hurt them,

23:56.227 --> 23:58.729
slow them down even.
That's gonna make going down

23:58.813 --> 24:00.189
into those tunnels
a whole lot safer.

24:00.273 --> 24:02.233
Okay, and who's gonna
be the one running out here

24:02.316 --> 24:03.234
with that thing?

24:03.317 --> 24:04.443
I am.

24:12.076 --> 24:13.828
Hello?

24:13.911 --> 24:16.122
-Anyone home?
-[knocking]

24:22.211 --> 24:24.046
Tabitha?

24:24.130 --> 24:27.049
I need to talk to you.

24:28.593 --> 24:29.635
[sighs]

24:34.891 --> 24:35.892
Hello?

25:11.761 --> 25:13.221
[exhales shakily]

25:20.603 --> 25:25.566
[beeping]

25:27.318 --> 25:30.154
[ominous music plays]

25:34.909 --> 25:37.745
[beeping rapidly]

25:39.664 --> 25:41.916
-[gasps]
-[beeping stops]

25:47.213 --> 25:48.589
Ah.

25:53.386 --> 25:55.304
[somber music plays]

25:56.973 --> 25:58.724
[birds singing]

26:04.438 --> 26:07.566
Is that the car the man in
the yellow suit came here in?

26:07.650 --> 26:09.110
Yeah.

26:09.193 --> 26:11.320
So, what kind of clues are we
looking for?

26:11.404 --> 26:12.822
[Victor] I don't know.

26:12.905 --> 26:14.699
Let's start with the trunk.

26:26.002 --> 26:27.962
[metal creaking]

26:34.844 --> 26:36.304
That's not that scary.

26:57.199 --> 26:59.368
Is that Miranda's car?

27:00.828 --> 27:02.288
Yeah.

27:04.373 --> 27:06.375
[metal creaking]

27:58.469 --> 27:59.929
[gasps]

28:06.227 --> 28:08.020
Can we go inside?

28:08.104 --> 28:11.357
No, honey, I don't think
it's a good idea.

28:11.440 --> 28:12.775
Why not?

28:22.368 --> 28:23.702
Mom?

28:25.121 --> 28:26.163
[Victor]
We should go.

28:26.247 --> 28:27.415
Did you find something?

28:27.498 --> 28:29.250
[Victor] We have to go.
We have to go right now!

28:29.333 --> 28:30.334
Victor, what did you find?

28:30.418 --> 28:33.129
A bag of teeth.

28:33.212 --> 28:34.505
-[Tabitha] A what?
-There was--

28:34.588 --> 28:37.758
Here, you should see them.
Here!

28:37.842 --> 28:38.843
No, no!

28:38.926 --> 28:40.219
No, he needs
to be prepared.

28:40.302 --> 28:42.263
Okay, wait.
Prepared for what?

28:42.346 --> 28:44.473
-He has to be, because--
-Wait!

28:44.557 --> 28:45.975
Are you really my mother?

28:47.977 --> 28:49.186
-Victor--
-Don't you see?

28:49.270 --> 28:51.063
Don't-- Did--
You came to town last time.

28:51.147 --> 28:53.482
You brought a boy and a girl,
and the man in yellow showed up.

28:53.566 --> 28:56.026
Everyone died,
but not the boy!

28:56.110 --> 28:57.778
The boy lived.

28:57.862 --> 29:00.239
And he grew up alone
and afraid.

29:00.322 --> 29:02.783
And he wasn't prepared.

29:02.867 --> 29:04.910
And now you're here with a boy
and a girl again,

29:04.994 --> 29:06.245
and the man in yellow
is back.

29:06.328 --> 29:08.164
-Mom, what does that mean?
-No, it's fine--

29:08.247 --> 29:10.332
-You have to be prepared, Ethan.
-Hey, Victor.

29:10.416 --> 29:12.376
-You have to know what's coming.
-No, Victor.

29:12.460 --> 29:15.171
You need to stop! Stop it!
Stop it! Ethan!

29:19.133 --> 29:21.010
What's wrong with you?

29:23.262 --> 29:24.388
Ethan!

29:37.526 --> 29:40.988
-[knocking]
-Oh, hey. Come in.

29:41.071 --> 29:43.532
Sorry, I didn't mean
to bother you.

29:43.616 --> 29:46.243
No, no.
No bother at all.

29:46.327 --> 29:47.953
What can I do for you?

29:48.037 --> 29:50.456
It's just, um...

29:50.539 --> 29:53.042
I was thinking about what you
said earlier this morning.

29:53.125 --> 29:55.336
About-- About going down
into those tunnels

29:55.419 --> 29:57.046
to dig up those bones.

29:58.631 --> 30:00.132
Isn't that dangerous?

30:02.218 --> 30:05.513
Uh, well, yeah.

30:05.596 --> 30:07.306
Yeah, it is.

30:07.389 --> 30:10.309
But it could also be
what helps us get home.

30:10.392 --> 30:11.477
How?

30:11.560 --> 30:13.521
Well, we're not quite clear
on that yet.

30:13.604 --> 30:15.314
But those things
that come out at night,

30:15.397 --> 30:17.483
people-- people say that they
live in those tunnels.

30:17.566 --> 30:18.901
That's right, yeah.

30:18.984 --> 30:23.322
So, if those bones are
important, it's not like

30:23.405 --> 30:24.990
they're just gonna let you go
down there and take them.

30:25.074 --> 30:27.159
No, they're not. But...
[clears throat]

30:27.243 --> 30:31.080
...it turns out, we might have
a new card to play.

30:32.331 --> 30:33.958
Remember this morning
when I said that

30:34.041 --> 30:35.626
Tabitha used one of these
to kill that doll

30:35.709 --> 30:36.835
out by the settlement?

30:36.919 --> 30:37.962
Yeah.

30:38.045 --> 30:39.421
Well, tonight,
we're gonna see

30:39.505 --> 30:41.882
what they do to those things
that come out of the woods.

30:41.966 --> 30:50.307
Really?

30:50.391 --> 30:54.228
Is there a reason we can't just
draw a map of the tunnels?

30:54.311 --> 30:57.439
I work better spatially.

30:57.523 --> 30:59.900
It's a technique I used when
I was designing my company.

30:59.984 --> 31:01.860
All right? If you
visualize the dimension

31:01.944 --> 31:03.529
of what you're tryin'
to create, right,

31:03.612 --> 31:05.364
the space you want
to move through,

31:05.447 --> 31:07.491
it helps create
a more accurate--

31:07.575 --> 31:10.953
Yeah, we're not exactly
designing a company. Right?

31:11.036 --> 31:12.079
It doesn't matter.

31:12.162 --> 31:14.039
You apply the principles
of what you know.

31:14.123 --> 31:15.207
Okay.

31:15.291 --> 31:19.295
Wait! What did you do before
you got here?

31:19.378 --> 31:21.547
-What?
-Before you came to town.

31:21.630 --> 31:23.549
What did you do?
What was your job?

31:23.632 --> 31:25.050
Can we please just focus?

31:25.134 --> 31:27.094
Oh, come on,
you know what I did.

31:27.177 --> 31:28.554
Yes.
Yes, I know what you did.

31:28.637 --> 31:30.264
Everyone knows what you did,
because...

31:30.347 --> 31:31.932
you never shut
the fuck up about it.

31:32.016 --> 31:33.559
If I guess,
will you tell me if I'm right?

31:33.642 --> 31:34.685
-No.
-Firefighter.

31:34.768 --> 31:38.355
-No.
-Manager at a retail store.

31:38.439 --> 31:40.274
Why-- Why are those your
first two guesses?

31:40.357 --> 31:42.443
Well, I--

31:42.526 --> 31:45.362
That's a lot of wires.

31:45.446 --> 31:47.281
Yeah, we're kind of
in the middle of...

31:47.364 --> 31:49.199
[Henry]
Well, don't let me stop you.

31:49.283 --> 31:51.327
What do you think Kenny did
before he got here?

31:51.410 --> 31:54.246
Okay.
I worked in youth sports.

31:54.330 --> 31:57.041
-You were a coach?
-No. I was an administrator.

31:57.124 --> 31:59.168
-Coach Kenny. I like that.
-No. Stop,

31:59.251 --> 32:01.170
can we just focus
on the maps.

32:01.253 --> 32:02.421
-[door opening]
-[Ellis] Hey.

32:02.504 --> 32:04.340
-How's it going?
-Kenny was a coach.

32:04.423 --> 32:05.424
Oh my God.

32:05.507 --> 32:06.967
We gotta get you a whistle.

32:07.051 --> 32:09.219
Great, uh, hey, Kenny,
can I talk to you outside?

32:09.303 --> 32:11.180
Yeah.

32:12.681 --> 32:14.308
[door opening]

32:20.606 --> 32:24.109
Hey, Henry. What'd you do
before you got here?

32:24.193 --> 32:26.236
Pretty much what
I'm doing right now.

32:37.706 --> 32:40.459
[goats bleating]

32:55.265 --> 32:58.310
[clucking]

33:13.409 --> 33:15.077
[inhaling]

33:20.749 --> 33:22.084
[inhaling]

33:27.172 --> 33:29.508
[ominous music plays]

33:44.815 --> 33:47.526
[indistinct chattering]

33:47.609 --> 33:49.194
[Elgin]
I'll be there in a second.

33:55.492 --> 33:56.618
Hi.

33:58.662 --> 34:00.706
What are you guys doing?

34:00.789 --> 34:03.083
Uh, we're just going through
some stuff in the storeroom.

34:04.668 --> 34:06.295
Mind if I sit?

34:08.172 --> 34:09.339
Okay.

34:14.511 --> 34:17.556
Uh, I never got
the chance to say

34:17.639 --> 34:21.310
how sorry I was
about your dad.

34:25.313 --> 34:27.733
Uh, how's your eye?

34:27.815 --> 34:29.359
Hm?

34:29.443 --> 34:33.822
-I mean--
-Oh, I know what you mean.

34:33.906 --> 34:37.074
Kristi says it's
healing pretty good.

34:39.703 --> 34:42.748
You gonna tell me
what happened?

34:42.831 --> 34:44.123
No.

34:49.963 --> 34:52.216
So, I guess you heard
about my mom.

34:53.675 --> 34:54.717
Do you think it's true?

34:56.594 --> 34:58.514
She thinks it is.

34:58.597 --> 35:00.224
And that scares
the shit out of me.

35:00.307 --> 35:01.433
But why?

35:01.517 --> 35:03.268
'Cause every time someone
here feels

35:03.352 --> 35:04.770
like they have a purpose,

35:04.853 --> 35:07.272
or that they've discovered
the truth,

35:07.356 --> 35:08.690
somebody always
ends up dead.

35:10.651 --> 35:12.778
But there is a truth here.

35:12.861 --> 35:14.363
-I mean, there has to be.
-Why?

35:15.739 --> 35:18.116
Why can't this whole
place just be some

35:18.200 --> 35:21.495
random fucking cruelty that
exists for no reason

35:21.578 --> 35:23.372
other than to do exactly
what it's doing?

35:23.455 --> 35:25.290
Look, I know you wanna believe
that this is all

35:25.374 --> 35:26.792
some part of God's
fucked-up plan--

35:26.875 --> 35:29.378
-I do.
-Okay, great,

35:29.461 --> 35:31.380
so explain to me
why you don't have an eye.

35:32.881 --> 35:34.550
We are all being tested.

35:34.633 --> 35:37.386
So, part of your test is
getting mutilated?

35:43.350 --> 35:44.476
Sorry...

35:47.563 --> 35:48.689
I'm an asshole.

35:49.898 --> 35:52.860
There is a truth
behind all of this.

35:55.904 --> 35:58.448
But you know
how this place wins?

35:58.532 --> 36:00.284
It's by throwing
so many lies at you

36:00.367 --> 36:02.369
that you don't believe
the truth

36:02.452 --> 36:04.454
even when it's staring you
right in the face.

36:17.759 --> 36:21.305
It isn't right what you're
doing, you know.

36:22.431 --> 36:23.682
So you said.

36:23.765 --> 36:26.560
Yeah, filling people's heads
with nonsense.

36:26.643 --> 36:30.689
I mean, telling my son
that his mother is--

36:30.772 --> 36:32.941
well, it isn't right.

36:47.497 --> 36:50.918
Have you talked
to Tabitha yet?

36:51.001 --> 36:54.004
Have I talked to the woman you
claim is a reincarnation

36:54.087 --> 36:56.548
of my dead wife?

36:56.632 --> 36:57.633
[sighs]

36:57.716 --> 37:00.928
No, I haven't
had the chance.

37:01.011 --> 37:03.805
She was out earlier
when I stopped by.

37:05.474 --> 37:07.267
[putting glass down]

37:07.351 --> 37:09.353
You know maybe if you cut
down a little on the--

37:09.436 --> 37:11.271
[beeping]

37:11.355 --> 37:12.439
What?
What is it?

37:12.522 --> 37:14.483
Do you hear that?

37:14.566 --> 37:15.525
Uh--

37:15.609 --> 37:18.487
[beeping]

37:18.570 --> 37:21.615
-He's back.
-[Henry groans]

37:21.698 --> 37:25.953
Henry, blink twice
if you can hear me.

37:26.036 --> 37:27.371
[groans]

37:27.454 --> 37:29.039
V--

37:29.122 --> 37:30.290
Dad?

37:30.374 --> 37:31.375
Wha--?

37:31.458 --> 37:33.335
Dad. Dad.

37:34.586 --> 37:35.504
Hi.

37:36.755 --> 37:38.882
-V--
-Dad. Stay with me.

37:38.966 --> 37:39.925
[Jade] Henry!

37:40.008 --> 37:41.426
-Henry.
-[snapping]

37:41.510 --> 37:44.054
Hey, Henry. What is it?
What just happened?

37:44.137 --> 37:46.765
Huh?
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa.

37:46.848 --> 37:47.808
What just happened?

37:51.019 --> 37:52.521
I need to go.

38:01.822 --> 38:02.823
[sniffing]

38:05.450 --> 38:06.451
Let me do it.

38:06.535 --> 38:07.661
What?

38:07.744 --> 38:09.413
Let me be the one
to go outside.

38:09.496 --> 38:10.956
[Boyd] No, look,
you've done enough.

38:11.039 --> 38:12.457
I just need to make sure that

38:12.541 --> 38:14.376
people are standing by their
doors to let me in.

38:14.459 --> 38:15.711
Just in case things
go sideways.

38:15.794 --> 38:17.379
I killed my brother.

38:17.462 --> 38:18.797
I tried to murder
a little boy.

38:18.880 --> 38:21.508
Nothing I do
will ever be enough.

38:22.718 --> 38:25.804
Well, tonight
is your night off.

38:25.887 --> 38:28.515
We go down into those tunnels,
that's when I'll need you.

38:30.851 --> 38:33.520
Be careful, Boyd.

38:33.603 --> 38:36.565
You just make sure you're
standing by that door, okay?

38:40.444 --> 38:44.406
[door creaking]

39:12.893 --> 39:17.814
[indistinct incantation]

39:34.706 --> 39:36.958
[whispering]
It's time to play.

39:38.168 --> 39:40.796
[tense music plays]

39:54.101 --> 39:59.022
[bell ringing]

40:06.113 --> 40:08.573
-[indistinct chatter]
-Okay.

40:08.657 --> 40:09.866
Nice.

40:11.243 --> 40:13.078
Hey. Hey.
What are you doing?

40:13.161 --> 40:15.831
Yoga. The fuck does it look
like I'm doing?

40:15.914 --> 40:18.917
Let's get back in bed.

40:19.000 --> 40:20.502
Please.

40:22.170 --> 40:23.130
Okay.

40:25.298 --> 40:30.887
[quietly] Driving me
fuckin' insane.

40:30.971 --> 40:32.139
[sighs]

40:33.932 --> 40:36.101
What are you even
doing down here?

40:36.184 --> 40:37.519
I thought you
were upstairs

40:37.602 --> 40:39.771
working on that project
of yours.

40:39.855 --> 40:41.606
We're a little
short-handed.

40:41.690 --> 40:43.859
Ellis and Kenny
are helping Boyd in town.

40:43.942 --> 40:46.111
Right.

40:46.194 --> 40:47.445
[sighs]

40:47.529 --> 40:49.948
I can't just fucking
lay here anymore.

40:50.031 --> 40:51.783
Okay, well you have to.

40:51.867 --> 40:53.577
At least for now.

40:53.660 --> 40:54.995
-[Donna sighs]
-I'm sorry.

40:55.078 --> 40:56.788
No, you're not.

40:56.872 --> 40:59.082
Your bedside manner sucks.

40:59.166 --> 41:01.042
[exhales]

41:01.126 --> 41:04.671
Donna, if this thing
with Jade and Tabitha,

41:04.754 --> 41:08.216
if that's real, after
everything you've survived here,

41:08.300 --> 41:10.594
you really wanna die right
before we all get to go home

41:10.677 --> 41:12.846
because you were too stubborn
to lay in bed for a minute?

41:12.929 --> 41:15.599
You never used
to be this sassy.

41:15.682 --> 41:19.019
Yeah, well, I gave birth
to a fucking monster, so,

41:19.102 --> 41:20.187
people change.

41:23.982 --> 41:26.818
Yeah, they do.

41:28.987 --> 41:31.114
[indistinct chatter]

41:31.198 --> 41:32.240
[door opening]

41:34.701 --> 41:35.827
You're staying here tonight?

41:35.911 --> 41:37.662
[Sophia]
Is-- Is that okay?

41:37.746 --> 41:40.081
I, um, I heard what Boyd was
planning in town

41:40.165 --> 41:41.917
and I would just rather
not be down there tonight.

41:43.710 --> 41:45.670
Those creatures
terrify me.

41:45.754 --> 41:46.838
Well, you're not alone.

41:46.922 --> 41:48.006
Welcome
to Colony House.

41:48.089 --> 41:49.799
Thank you.

41:49.883 --> 41:52.552
[bell ringing]

41:52.636 --> 41:54.179
Hey, he tell you the plan?

41:55.639 --> 41:56.932
Yeah.

41:57.015 --> 41:59.184
All right. I talked to
everybody in all the houses.

41:59.267 --> 42:00.810
-We're all set.
-Okay.

42:00.894 --> 42:02.062
Let's get ready.

42:08.610 --> 42:09.778
All right.

42:14.324 --> 42:17.911
I figure we'll give 'em an hour
or so after nightfall.

42:17.994 --> 42:19.079
[sighs]

42:19.162 --> 42:21.206
[Boyd] Let 'em get settled
out there.

42:21.289 --> 42:24.084
Make 'em think it's just
a normal night.

42:25.252 --> 42:26.169
Dad.

42:28.964 --> 42:29.965
What's goin' on?

42:30.048 --> 42:31.633
Um.

42:31.716 --> 42:33.301
I should be the one to go out
there tonight.

42:33.385 --> 42:35.971
-What? No.
-[Ellis clears throat]

42:36.054 --> 42:37.931
Hey, look,
it makes more sense.

42:38.014 --> 42:38.932
Why?

42:39.015 --> 42:40.350
[Kenny]
I'm your second.

42:40.433 --> 42:42.602
Right? I'm your second now,
and these are the things

42:42.686 --> 42:44.854
that I'm supposed to do so you
don't have to. That's why.

42:44.938 --> 42:48.316
No. I appreciate it,
but it's my plan, my risk.

42:48.400 --> 42:49.943
Dad, what if something
goes wrong?

42:50.026 --> 42:51.236
We can't afford
to lose you here.

42:51.319 --> 42:52.946
Oh, oh, so we can afford
to lose Kenny?

42:53.029 --> 42:54.823
That's not what he's saying.
You know that.

42:54.906 --> 42:56.992
Listen, we're not having
this conversation.

42:57.075 --> 42:58.159
Dad--

42:58.243 --> 43:00.078
I am not having this
conversation!

43:00.161 --> 43:02.789
Dad, you can't
fuckin' do it!

43:02.872 --> 43:05.709
Look, it's not safe for you to
go out there.

43:05.792 --> 43:07.168
Not in your condition.

43:07.252 --> 43:08.753
My--

43:08.837 --> 43:12.799
Okay, what happens, what if
your leg gives out? Huh?

43:12.882 --> 43:15.051
Like last time? What if you
can't get back up this time?

43:15.135 --> 43:18.763
Listen to me very carefully.
Both of you, listen!

43:18.847 --> 43:21.266
I'm not sending anyone out
there and risk their life

43:21.349 --> 43:23.143
while I sit
in here like a--

43:23.226 --> 43:25.312
fucking, stop it!

43:25.395 --> 43:27.731
Goddammit!
Stop it!

43:37.782 --> 43:38.867
Dad, please?

43:44.289 --> 43:45.957
Please.

43:49.794 --> 43:52.672
[swing creaking]

43:57.218 --> 43:59.137
We've got
a few more coming.

43:59.220 --> 44:01.056
[Boyd] Where?

44:01.139 --> 44:03.224
[Ellis] Right there.

44:03.308 --> 44:04.726
You see 'em?

44:06.770 --> 44:08.229
Yeah.
I got 'em.

44:09.814 --> 44:12.359
Look, you remember:

44:12.442 --> 44:14.944
if you can't make it back
into the station,

44:15.028 --> 44:17.364
you got escape routes
up and down the street.

44:17.447 --> 44:19.991
Every house has got somebody
waiting at the door for you.

44:20.075 --> 44:22.118
And if you can't make it
to one of those houses,

44:22.202 --> 44:24.204
we got talismans on the church,
the bus,

44:24.287 --> 44:26.247
the diner, and the barn.

44:26.331 --> 44:31.044
So you find the safest route you
can and, hey, you run.

44:31.127 --> 44:32.045
I got it.

44:33.838 --> 44:34.756
Kenny, look at me.

44:39.469 --> 44:42.013
I'll be okay.

44:42.097 --> 44:44.015
All right.

44:44.099 --> 44:46.851
Okay. Okay.

44:47.769 --> 44:50.355
[Ellis] Hey, we got one or two
more coming up the road.

44:52.107 --> 44:54.192
[tense music plays]

44:54.275 --> 45:00.198
[indistinct incantation]

45:07.122 --> 45:10.083
[indistinct incantation]

45:12.127 --> 45:16.714
[breathing rapidly]

45:32.480 --> 45:35.024
[muffled screaming]

45:35.108 --> 45:38.319
[flesh tearing]

45:38.403 --> 45:41.406
Yeah, I think
we got one.

45:41.489 --> 45:44.409
[Boyd] Still too far.
Wait till he's closer.

45:44.492 --> 45:45.994
Boyd,
that's close enough!

45:46.077 --> 45:48.538
[Ellis] Okay. Okay, the rest of
them are spread out.

45:48.621 --> 45:51.082
It's a good time;
let's go!

45:51.166 --> 45:52.792
Hey.
I'm ready.

45:52.876 --> 45:55.336
Fast and dirty.

45:55.420 --> 45:57.422
You stab, you run.

45:57.505 --> 46:00.341
Don't wait
to see what happens.

46:03.553 --> 46:05.972
You ready?

46:06.055 --> 46:07.140
-Yeah.
-Three, two...

46:15.148 --> 46:16.566
[breathing heavily]

46:16.649 --> 46:20.028
-[grunts]
-[screams]

46:20.111 --> 46:22.071
-I think it worked!
-All right. Come on--

46:22.155 --> 46:24.908
[screaming]

46:26.576 --> 46:30.788
[screaming]

46:33.583 --> 46:34.918
[gasps]

46:36.878 --> 46:37.879
Just kidding.

46:43.259 --> 46:46.262
[grunting]

46:46.346 --> 46:47.388
[guts squelching]

46:47.472 --> 46:50.308
[Boyd]
Get outta there!

46:50.391 --> 46:51.976
[Ellis] Dad, they're
blocking the doors!

46:52.060 --> 46:53.978
No!

46:54.062 --> 46:56.272
This isn't going very well,
is it?

47:07.075 --> 47:10.328
[grunts]

47:23.258 --> 47:24.467
[gasps]

47:33.101 --> 47:34.561
[gasps]

47:38.106 --> 47:40.275
[breathing heavily]

47:48.950 --> 47:50.285
[door banging]

47:53.413 --> 47:56.124
I think you have a problem,
Kenny.

48:13.141 --> 48:14.225
Oh, no.

48:18.646 --> 48:21.149
I killed your father,
you know.

48:23.610 --> 48:27.363
He made such funny noises.

48:27.447 --> 48:29.032
No. No. No. No.

48:31.659 --> 48:33.911
Do you make funny noises?

48:33.995 --> 48:35.538
[breathing unsteadily]

48:36.706 --> 48:38.416
[roars]

48:38.499 --> 48:42.045
-Stop!
-[stops shouting]

48:42.128 --> 48:44.380
[grunts]

48:47.467 --> 48:49.385
[gasps]

48:55.600 --> 48:59.270
[gasping]

49:02.190 --> 49:03.650
[screaming]

49:03.733 --> 49:06.361
[thudding]

49:08.154 --> 49:11.949
-[screaming]
-[bell ringing]

49:12.033 --> 49:13.284
-[smashing]
-[screaming]

49:13.368 --> 49:15.620
[roars]

49:15.703 --> 49:17.330
The door! The door!

49:17.413 --> 49:18.748
[roars]

49:18.831 --> 49:22.251
[indistinct screams]

49:22.335 --> 49:25.129
[screaming]

49:25.213 --> 49:26.714
[roars]

49:28.132 --> 49:29.467
Roger!
Please don't do this!

49:29.550 --> 49:31.469
-I know you're in there!
-[roars]

49:31.552 --> 49:34.305
I know
you're still inside!

49:34.389 --> 49:35.723
I know you're still in there!

49:37.725 --> 49:40.103
-[grunting with effort]
-[roars in pain]

49:40.186 --> 49:42.522
[screaming]

49:46.567 --> 49:49.487
What the fuck just happened?!

49:49.570 --> 49:53.491
What just happened?

49:53.574 --> 49:55.702
[frantic music plays]

49:58.746 --> 50:00.707
[theme music playing]
